WEBVTT

NOTE calculation-questions: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.200
Identical suggestions,
missing values and stale scans:

V0-2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.240
three things that look
like bugs, and are not.

V1a-1
00:00:14.023 --> 00:00:16.568
When the required amount
exceeds the daily maximum,

V1a-2
00:00:16.668 --> 00:00:19.513
every station above the cap
lands on the same percentage.

V1b-1
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.770
A run of identical numbers means
the cap is deciding, not the scan.

V2a-1
00:00:30.683 --> 00:00:33.402
The maximum possible
suggestion is the daily

V2a-2
00:00:33.502 --> 00:00:36.283
maximum divided by the
Lynx reference amount.

V2b-1
00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:39.109
Change either number
and the ceiling moves,

V2b-2
00:00:39.209 --> 00:00:42.703
which is the honest fix if the
ceiling is too low for your course.

V3a-1
00:00:49.977 --> 00:00:52.333
A dash means there is nothing to show:

V3a-2
00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:55.287
no current scan, and no
modelled value either.

V3b-1
00:00:55.793 --> 00:00:59.568
It is not zero, and it is not
an error in the calculation.

V3b-2
00:00:59.668 --> 00:01:02.403
The station has no data to calculate from.

V4a-1
00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:12.474
A greyed, italic average means
the value came from the model,

V4a-2
00:01:12.574 --> 00:01:14.450
rather than a scan taken that day.

V4b-1
00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.440
The calculation still runs,
but it is running on an estimate.

V5a-1
00:01:26.983 --> 00:01:31.608
The diagnostics dialog reports whether
the organisation has TurfRad access,

V5a-2
00:01:31.708 --> 00:01:35.163
whether it has scan data at
all, and the last scan date.

V5b-1
00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:39.472
If access and scan data are both
fine and only the date is old,

V5b-2
00:01:39.572 --> 00:01:43.982
use Request latest scan data in the
toolbar. It cannot make TurfRad scan,

V5b-3
00:01:44.082 --> 00:01:47.587
so if TurfRad has nothing newer,
the date will not change.
